WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.160
Welcome to привет, русский!

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.940
Эписот 60-сидьей, 4-двадцать седьмой июля 2026 года.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.560
I am allia, and today we are going to learn some really fun Russian words, ready?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:12.620
Поехали!

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.000
That means let's go!

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.940
Today our word of the day is путешествия, путешествия, путешествия, путешествия

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.540
СТЕ, it means journey or trip.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.680
Imagine stitching together memories on a long journey.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.060
That helps you remember путешествия.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.320
Repeat after me, путешествия.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.460
Now let's use it, я люблю путешествия на поезде.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.780
That means I love a journey by train.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.740
Let's build more travel words.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.900
First, билет, билет, билет, it means ticket, repeat after me, билет.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.880
Try this sentence, мне нужен билет в Москву.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.120
That means I need a ticket to Moscow.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.660
Next comes чемодан.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.700
чемодан чех-мат-дан.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.720
It means suitcase, repeat after me, чемодан.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.560
You can say, чемодан тяжелый, that means the suitcase is heavy.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.540
Now we have passport, passport, PHS port.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.360
It means passport, repeat after me, passport.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.120
A simple phrase is, покажи passport, that means show your passport.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.460
Next is a tell.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.700
A tell a tear, it means hotel, repeat after me, a tell.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.760
We say, мы ждем в отеле, that means we live in a hotel.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:26.080
Next is samolod, samolod, сахмах лиод, it means airplane, repeat after me, samolod.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.040
You can say, самолёт летает, that means the airplane flies.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.320
Remember that, летает, means flies.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.700
And the airplane does exactly that.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.620
The memory hook connects the world to the action of flying high above the clouds.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.800
Try repeating the full sentence three times to walk it in.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.140
Let's learn вокзал, вокзал, вок, сах, it means train station.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:54.080
Repeat after me, вокзал, you can say, поезд на вокзале, that means the train is at the station.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:03.320
Now comes рюкзак, рюкзак, рюкзак, рюкзах, рюкзах, рюкзах, рюкзах, рюкзах, рюкзах на спине.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.720
That means the backpack is on the back.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.580
Finally we have карта, карта, ки-артах.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:16.740
It means map, repeat after me, карта, a useful phrase is, дай мне карту, that means give me the map.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.000
Now for a quick grammar byte.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.100
In Russian, we use the little word вы, to show you are going somewhere.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.780
It works like the English word too.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:33.440
You say, я еду в Москву, that means I am going to Moscow, or my idome hotel, that means we are going to the hotel.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:38.660
The ending of the place often changes a little, but the word вы stays the same,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.520
want to know secret about one of today's words.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.720
The Russian word passport and the English word passport are actually the same word.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.000
They both come from the French passport, which meant pass through the port.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.620
The word traveled across Europe with traders and sailors.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:03:00.040
It reached Russian in the 1700s, when Peter the Great opened Russia to the world.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:06.000
Be careful though, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine, but really means shop.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.000
Next time you hold your passport, remember it shares a story with Russian passport.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:17.340
That connection started in medieval French and gives you a secret shortcut for remembering the word forever.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.340
Russian love long-trained journey across their huge country.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.560
The famous Transseberian railway takes seven days from Moscow to Vladivostok.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.360
Families often bring big tomatoes full of food for the trip.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.020
The journey crosses many time zones and vast landscapes.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.980
passengers spend days watching the scenery change outside the window.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.600
These long rides turn travel into a shared family experience with plenty of snacks along the way.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.620
Let's practice. Do you remember what bilet means?

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:51.100
It means ticket. Try saying, I need bilet three times today.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.280
For kids, draw your dream trip and label the Somaliot, Rukzak and Karta in Russian.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.860
For adults, practice the phrases at an imaginary airport.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:04.180
By saying, I need bilet and package passport out loud three times.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.780
These exercises have both children and grownups, turn new words into real habits.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.920
Молодец, that means well done.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.840
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.400
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.560
And you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.540
See you next time.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.060
Пока!

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.440
That's Russian for buy.

